              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p>The notation layer is a node like any other: it is where every
  symbol in the forest is defined, and it is the only place a macro may
  be introduced. Read <fr:link href="/ffi/preamble/" title="Forest preamble: the notation layer" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/preamble/" display-uri="preamble" type="local">Forest preamble: the notation layer</fr:link> for the index of the seven notation
  nodes, the mechanics of forester's
  <html:code><![CDATA[\def]]></html:code>, and the list of glyphs that
  currently carry two meanings.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
