                <fr:title text="Conventions">Conventions</fr:title>
              </fr:frontmatter>
              <fr:mainmatter>
                <html:p><html:strong>Addresses.</html:strong> Statement nodes are <html:code>ffi-NNNN</html:code>, assigned
  in order of minting and never reassigned. Infrastructure —
  <fr:link href="/ffi/preamble/" title="Forest preamble: the notation layer" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/preamble/" display-uri="preamble" type="local">Forest preamble: the notation layer</fr:link>, the seven <html:code>macros-</html:code> nodes, this index — keeps
  readable addresses, because it is named after what it is rather than
  after a claim that might be restated.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>Taxon and tags.</html:strong> The taxon is the grammatical kind:
  definition, theorem, proposition, lemma, corollary, conjecture,
  principle, notation, reference. Tags carry area — foundations,
  symplectic, height, growth, frontier — and status: proven, open,
  conditional, refuted. A node tagged refuted is still a node; it is on
  the record because the refutation is a result.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>One claim per node.</html:strong> If a node states two things, it is two
  nodes. This is why the address space is sparse rather than
  hierarchical: splitting a node mints new addresses and leaves the old
  one in place, pointing forward.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>Dependencies.</html:strong> Every node carries
  <html:code><![CDATA[\import{preamble}]]></html:code> for notation and
  nothing else; each mathematical dependency is a link in the
  <html:code><![CDATA[\uses{...}]]></html:code> line, because forester derives
  its backlink graph from links and not from imports. Until proof nodes
  exist, that line carries what a proof's inline citations would.
  <html:code>./check-dag.py</html:code> verifies that every link resolves, that the
  graph is acyclic, and that nothing is stranded.</html:p>
                <html:p><html:strong>Provenance.</html:strong> Every statement node ends with a line pointing
  into the journal and the experiment record. Full proofs live in the
  journal; proof nodes are a later pass.</html:p>
              </fr:mainmatter>
            </fr:tree>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
